        "id": 1589902
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T17:33:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This type of function should no longer be necessary with class template argument deduction.\n\nSomething like this:\n```\ntemplate \u003ctypename State, size_t kNumTransitions\u003e\nFsmConfig(State starting_state, std::array\u003cTransition\u003cState\u003e, kNumTransitions\u003e transitions) -\u003e FsmConfig\u003cState, kNumTransitions\u003e;\n```\n\nThen, you can declare `FsmConfig` without template arguments, and it will deduce them.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 346,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 351,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "17c3d0573efc7e4e9254372d08c4a2592424dd37",
